1
00:00:00,059 --> 00:00:01,769
Welcome to Rez grid Academy.

2
00:00:02,170 --> 00:00:05,860
In this lesson, we will match
subscription capacity to the roster.

3
00:00:06,269 --> 00:00:10,539
Large onboarding can stop at personnel
or unit limits when capacity has

4
00:00:10,539 --> 00:00:12,210
not been reviewed in advance.

5
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:15,699
We will explain the features,
the setup decisions, and a

6
00:00:15,699 --> 00:00:17,620
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:17,819 --> 00:00:22,450
Before inviting 40 new members, an
administrator confirms the plan has room

8
00:00:22,629 --> 00:00:24,870
or asks the managing member to change it.

9
00:00:25,370 --> 00:00:29,489
Adding members or units stops at the
plan limit, so check the remaining

10
00:00:29,489 --> 00:00:31,260
room before a large onboarding.

11
00:00:31,919 --> 00:00:35,370
The examples in this series use a
fictional department and are teaching

12
00:00:35,370 --> 00:00:37,589
scenarios, not default settings.

13
00:00:37,830 --> 00:00:39,470
Base plans and capacity.

14
00:00:39,910 --> 00:00:43,950
Your plan, its personnel and
unit limits, and your add-ons.

15
00:00:44,399 --> 00:00:47,919
Check the remaining room before
adding many members or units.

16
00:00:48,080 --> 00:00:50,839
For the training scenario,
work in this order.

17
00:00:51,310 --> 00:00:51,879
Step 1.

18
00:00:52,409 --> 00:00:56,269
Review the observed base plan,
personnel count, and unit count.

19
00:00:56,750 --> 00:00:57,409
Step 2.

20
00:00:57,920 --> 00:01:00,899
Compare planned onboarding
with available capacity.

21
00:01:01,319 --> 00:01:02,080
Step 3.

22
00:01:02,479 --> 00:01:06,500
Review add-on entitlements and their
separate configuration prerequisites.

23
00:01:06,679 --> 00:01:08,179
Now verify the result.

24
00:01:08,549 --> 00:01:12,000
Check observed subscription evidence
and current resource counts.

25
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:16,079
Use the owning billing screen for
any authorized subscription change.

26
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:19,820
A common problem to watch
for: Missing billing evidence

27
00:01:19,820 --> 00:01:21,579
means capacity is unknown.

28
00:01:21,999 --> 00:01:24,990
Only the managing member
performs subscription changes.

29
00:01:25,179 --> 00:01:26,730
Your practice task is simple.

30
00:01:27,209 --> 00:01:30,270
Compare current counts with
a proposed roster expansion.

31
00:01:30,699 --> 00:01:34,649
Document headroom and optional
add-ons without purchasing anything.

32
00:01:35,130 --> 00:01:39,029
Record the result, who owns the
follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

33
00:01:39,470 --> 00:01:42,759
Use the linked feature scripts for
the detailed screen recording plan.
